    <string name="google_privacy">How DayTrace uses Google</string>
    <string name="google_privacy_subtitle">What it can see, and what it never does</string>
    <string name="google_privacy_details">DayTrace asks Google only for what each integration needs.\n\n• Google Account: which account it is (its email address).\n• Google Calendar: the list of your calendars, and adding events to calendars you own. DayTrace can\'t see or change your other events.\n\nNothing is sent to Google without your OK, and only the event itself: its title, time, place and the note it came from. Never your recordings or your other notes.\n\nYou can disconnect here at any time, or at myaccount.google.com/permissions.</string>

